1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,760
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:03,880
Lesson 2: Earth Movement.

3
00:00:08,117 --> 00:00:09,637
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:13,377 --> 00:00:14,797
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:15,277 --> 00:00:16,457
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:16,537 --> 00:00:18,977
Understand that the Earth is spherical.

7
00:00:19,917 --> 00:00:22,077
Identify the two types of movements of

8
00:00:22,157 --> 00:00:22,537
the Earth.

9
00:00:23,197 --> 00:00:25,397
Explain rotation and its effects.

10
00:00:26,177 --> 00:00:28,557
Understand revolution and its effects.

11
00:00:29,417 --> 00:00:32,177
Learn about different seasons caused by revolution.

12
00:00:32,257 --> 00:00:36,157
Define solstices and equinoxes and when they

13
00:00:36,237 --> 00:00:36,557
occur.

14
00:00:38,495 --> 00:00:39,355
Start-Up Activity.

15
00:00:43,315 --> 00:00:45,295
Take a ball and spin it.

16
00:00:45,815 --> 00:00:46,815
Notice how it moves.

17
00:00:47,655 --> 00:00:49,615
Imagine this is the Earth moving in

18
00:00:49,695 --> 00:00:50,015
space.

19
00:00:50,795 --> 00:00:53,595
The Earth moves in two ways—let's explore

20
00:00:53,675 --> 00:00:55,195
these movements and their effects!

21
00:00:57,005 --> 00:00:58,665
Who proved that the earth is spherical?

22
00:01:03,165 --> 00:01:05,965
Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth

23
00:01:06,045 --> 00:01:06,605
was flat.

24
00:01:07,305 --> 00:01:10,705
However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of

25
00:01:10,785 --> 00:01:12,445
the first to suggest that the Earth

26
00:01:12,525 --> 00:01:13,145
is spherical.

27
00:01:14,205 --> 00:01:17,705
Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how

28
00:01:17,785 --> 00:01:20,525
ships disappear over the horizon and how

29
00:01:20,605 --> 00:01:22,465
the Earth's shadow on the Moon is

30
00:01:22,545 --> 00:01:24,305
curved during a lunar eclipse.

31
00:01:24,385 --> 00:01:28,225
Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further

32
00:01:28,305 --> 00:01:30,245
confirmed that the Earth is round.

33
00:01:32,031 --> 00:01:33,591
The Two Movements of the Earth.

34
00:01:37,611 --> 00:01:39,431
The Earth moves in two ways:

35
00:01:40,131 --> 00:01:41,971
Rotation – The Earth spins on its

36
00:01:42,051 --> 00:01:43,271
axis around itself.

37
00:01:44,471 --> 00:01:46,251
Revolution – The Earth moves around the

38
00:01:46,331 --> 00:01:46,651
Sun.

39
00:01:48,176 --> 00:01:48,856
Rotation.

40
00:01:53,176 --> 00:01:55,156
Rotation is the movement of the Earth

41
00:01:55,236 --> 00:01:57,396
around its own axis is called Rotation.

42
00:01:58,416 --> 00:02:00,196
The earth rotates from west to east.

43
00:02:00,776 --> 00:02:03,116
It completes one full rotation in 24

44
00:02:03,196 --> 00:02:03,516
hours.

45
00:02:04,256 --> 00:02:06,256
The speed of rotation is faster at

46
00:02:06,336 --> 00:02:07,976
the equator and slower at the poles.

47
00:02:08,736 --> 00:02:10,396
The axis is tilted at an angle

48
00:02:10,476 --> 00:02:12,126
of 23.5°.

49
00:02:12,256 --> 00:02:14,796
As the Earth is spherical in shape,

50
00:02:15,236 --> 00:02:16,956
only one half of the Earth receives

51
00:02:17,036 --> 00:02:18,116
sunlight at a time.

52
00:02:18,796 --> 00:02:20,756
Thus, the side of the Earth facing

53
00:02:20,836 --> 00:02:22,256
the Sun experience day.

54
00:02:22,936 --> 00:02:23,736
On the other hand,

55
00:02:23,936 --> 00:02:24,396
the other half,

56
00:02:24,716 --> 00:02:26,296
or the part away from the sun,

57
00:02:26,676 --> 00:02:27,856
experiences night.

58
00:02:28,616 --> 00:02:29,936
As the Earth rotates,

59
00:02:30,156 --> 00:02:32,176
the lighted part moves into the darkness.

60
00:02:33,176 --> 00:02:35,096
Rotation causes day and night.

61
00:02:36,791 --> 00:02:37,431
Do You Know?

62
00:02:41,611 --> 00:02:43,711
The Earth rotates at a speed of

63
00:02:44,341 --> 00:02:47,571
1,670 kilometers per hour at the equator,

64
00:02:48,051 --> 00:02:49,535
but we don’t feel it because we’re

65
00:02:49,615 --> 00:02:50,691
moving along with it!

66
00:02:52,275 --> 00:02:53,015
Revolution.

67
00:02:57,075 --> 00:02:59,215
Revolution is the movement of the Earth

68
00:02:59,295 --> 00:03:01,035
around the Sun in a fixed path

69
00:03:01,115 --> 00:03:01,835
called an orbit.

70
00:03:02,615 --> 00:03:04,315
The Earth revolves around the Sun in

71
00:03:04,395 --> 00:03:05,295
an elliptical orbit.

72
00:03:05,975 --> 00:03:09,915
It takes 365¼ days (one year) to

73
00:03:09,995 --> 00:03:11,055
complete one revolution.

74
00:03:11,995 --> 00:03:14,135
The tilt of the Earth's axis remains

75
00:03:14,215 --> 00:03:15,655
the same during revolution.

76
00:03:17,095 --> 00:03:18,815
Revolution causes seasonal changes.

77
00:03:18,895 --> 00:03:21,295
The revolution of the Earth and the

78
00:03:21,375 --> 00:03:23,555
tilt of its axis cause different seasons:

79
00:03:24,515 --> 00:03:26,335
Summer – The hemisphere tilted towards the

80
00:03:26,415 --> 00:03:27,895
Sun experiences summer.

81
00:03:28,455 --> 00:03:30,435
Winter – The hemisphere tilted away from

82
00:03:30,515 --> 00:03:32,275
the Sun experiences winter.

83
00:03:33,415 --> 00:03:35,535
Spring – Occurs between winter and summer

84
00:03:35,615 --> 00:03:37,595
when the temperature starts rising.

85
00:03:38,775 --> 00:03:40,775
Autumn – Occurs between summer and winter

86
00:03:40,855 --> 00:03:42,715
when the temperature starts dropping.

87
00:03:44,473 --> 00:03:45,493
Let's Learn More.

88
00:03:49,573 --> 00:03:52,053
A day on Earth is actually 23

89
00:03:52,133 --> 00:03:54,113
hours, 56 minutes,

90
00:03:54,693 --> 00:03:56,573
not exactly 24 hours,

91
00:03:57,093 --> 00:03:58,653
but we round it off to 24

92
00:03:58,733 --> 00:04:01,133
hours because it’s easier to keep track

93
00:04:01,213 --> 00:04:01,633
of time.

94
00:04:03,371 --> 00:04:05,191
What is Solstice and When Does It

95
00:04:05,271 --> 00:04:05,591
Occur?

96
00:04:09,751 --> 00:04:11,011
A solstice is a day,

97
00:04:11,091 --> 00:04:13,231
when the sun shines vertically over a

98
00:04:13,311 --> 00:04:16,111
Tropic (both cancer and Capricorn) in the

99
00:04:16,191 --> 00:04:18,051
afternoon and the day is the longest

100
00:04:18,131 --> 00:04:18,991
in that hemisphere.

101
00:04:19,811 --> 00:04:20,831
On 22 December,

102
00:04:21,091 --> 00:04:22,731
the rays of the sun fall directly

103
00:04:22,811 --> 00:04:24,311
over the Tropic of Capricorn.

104
00:04:25,031 --> 00:04:26,711
This is the longest day in Southern

105
00:04:26,791 --> 00:04:28,271
Hemisphere (summer season),

106
00:04:28,651 --> 00:04:29,891
while in the Northern Hemisphere,

107
00:04:30,291 --> 00:04:32,231
it is the shortest day (winter season).

108
00:04:32,311 --> 00:04:34,771
This is called 'Winter Solstice.

109
00:04:35,571 --> 00:04:36,631
On 21 June,

110
00:04:37,171 --> 00:04:39,131
sunlight falls vertically over the Tropic of

111
00:04:39,211 --> 00:04:39,531
Cancer.

112
00:04:39,851 --> 00:04:41,891
This is the longest day in Northern

113
00:04:41,971 --> 00:04:44,934
Hemisphere and hence it is called 'Summer

114
00:04:45,024 --> 00:04:47,071
Solstice', while in the Southern Hemisphere,

115
00:04:47,511 --> 00:04:48,711
it is the shortest day.

116
00:04:50,385 --> 00:04:51,385
Let's Learn More.

117
00:04:55,705 --> 00:04:57,905
Earth keeps rotating due to inertia,

118
00:04:58,445 --> 00:05:00,845
the same reason you continue moving forward

119
00:05:00,925 --> 00:05:02,385
when you stop a bike suddenly.

120
00:05:03,325 --> 00:05:05,885
This movement doesn’t stop because there’s no

121
00:05:05,965 --> 00:05:07,945
friction in space to slow it down!

122
00:05:09,603 --> 00:05:11,443
What is Equinox and When Does It

123
00:05:11,523 --> 00:05:11,843
Occur?

124
00:05:15,803 --> 00:05:18,183
The sun falls directly on the equator

125
00:05:18,263 --> 00:05:19,423
two times in a year.

126
00:05:20,103 --> 00:05:21,943
During this period there is equal length

127
00:05:22,023 --> 00:05:23,563
of day and night all over the

128
00:05:23,643 --> 00:05:23,963
world.

129
00:05:24,563 --> 00:05:25,523
In Northern Hemisphere,

130
00:05:25,843 --> 00:05:27,843
the March Equinox is called the Vernal

131
00:05:27,923 --> 00:05:30,723
or Spring Equinox while September Equinox is

132
00:05:30,803 --> 00:05:32,283
called Autumnal Equinox.

133
00:05:33,123 --> 00:05:36,623
Spring Equinox (March 21st) marks the beginning

134
00:05:36,703 --> 00:05:37,263
of spring.

135
00:05:37,343 --> 00:05:41,763
Autumn Equinox (September 23rd) marks the beginning

136
00:05:41,843 --> 00:05:42,363
of autumn.

137
00:05:44,155 --> 00:05:44,555
Recall.

138
00:05:44,635 --> 00:05:50,035
The Earth's movements,

139
00:05:50,575 --> 00:05:51,915
rotation and revolution,

140
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:54,575
have significant affects on our lives.

141
00:05:55,575 --> 00:05:57,635
Rotation causes day and night,

142
00:05:57,995 --> 00:06:00,035
while revolution leads to the change of

143
00:06:00,115 --> 00:06:00,455
seasons.

144
00:06:01,695 --> 00:06:04,295
Solstices and equinoxes mark the shift in

145
00:06:04,375 --> 00:06:06,895
seasons, playing an essential role in our

146
00:06:06,975 --> 00:06:08,255
climate and timekeeping.

147
00:06:09,968 --> 00:06:10,808
Let's Remember.

148
00:06:15,288 --> 00:06:16,748
The Earth moves in two ways:

149
00:06:17,608 --> 00:06:18,648
rotation and revolution.

150
00:06:19,588 --> 00:06:21,448
Rotation causes day and night,

151
00:06:21,768 --> 00:06:23,508
while revolution causes seasons.

152
00:06:24,368 --> 00:06:26,968
The Earth completes one rotation in 24

153
00:06:27,048 --> 00:06:31,468
hours and one revolution in 365¼ days.

154
00:06:32,368 --> 00:06:34,468
Solstices occur in June and December,

155
00:06:34,848 --> 00:06:36,748
marking the longest and shortest days.

156
00:06:37,628 --> 00:06:39,748
Equinoxes occur in March and September,

157
00:06:39,828 --> 00:06:41,688
when day and night are equal.

158
00:06:43,393 --> 00:06:44,233
Word Bank.

159
00:06:48,453 --> 00:06:50,593
Rotation – Spinning of the Earth on

160
00:06:50,673 --> 00:06:51,353
its axis.

161
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:54,013
Revolution – Movement of the Earth around

162
00:06:54,093 --> 00:06:54,493
the Sun.

163
00:06:54,963 --> 00:06:56,433
Orbit – The path of the Earth

164
00:06:56,513 --> 00:06:57,473
around the Sun.

165
00:06:57,553 --> 00:06:59,773
Solstice – When the Sun is at

166
00:06:59,853 --> 00:07:01,913
its farthest point north or south.

167
00:07:02,593 --> 00:07:04,413
Equinox – When day and night are

168
00:07:04,493 --> 00:07:04,813
equal.
